# /docs/ and /zh/docs/ are real pages now (src/pages/docs/index.astro and its
# [locale] twin), so only the bare site roots still redirect, and they land on
# the dashboard rather than on one article. The four /docs rules that used to
# forward to getting-started are gone: a redirect on a URL that has content
# would hide the highest-authority page on the site from both readers and
# crawlers. These rules belong here and not in astro.config.mjs: a static
# build turns `redirects` into meta-refresh stubs, which the browser paints
# for a frame before forwarding.
/ /docs/ 301
/zh /zh/docs/ 301
/zh/ /zh/docs/ 301

# Internal release process pages were accidentally published once. Keep these
# redirects so stale static paths cannot expose the old content again.
/docs/release-process /docs/ 302
/docs/release-process/ /docs/ 302
/zh/docs/release-process /zh/docs/ 302
/zh/docs/release-process/ /zh/docs/ 302
/:locale/docs/release-process /:locale/docs/ 302
/:locale/docs/release-process/ /:locale/docs/ 302

# Docs content exists in en/zh only (#534). The other app UI languages used
# to build as English-fallback pages with self canonicals; permanently
# redirect those URLs to the English path so the duplicates converge.
